#====================================================================
# E328 - Isolate MPICH wrapper flags from Worker-local CPPFLAGS
#====================================================================

id:                     E364
trigger_tool:           conan|configure|mpicc
phase:                  package
error_signature:        mpicc contains non-relocatable paths: /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local

severity:               2
category:               relocatable, autoconf, mpi, openharmony, wrapper
match_keywords:         MPICH, mpicc, WRAPPER_CPPFLAGS, CPPFLAGS, user-local include, non-relocatable path
title:                  Isolate generated MPI wrappers from Worker-local CPPFLAGS

root_cause:             MPICH configure copies the active CPPFLAGS into WRAPPER_CPPFLAGS. The OHOS Conan profile adds the Worker-only $HOME/usr/local/include path, so packaging embeds that absolute path in mpicc and the recipe's relocation guard rejects the package after the long build and upstream test run.
affected_scope:         Autoconf projects that persist build-time CPPFLAGS or equivalent environment flags into installed compiler wrappers or metadata.
verification_cmd:       Run the production recipe method with a poisoned Worker environment, require CPPFLAGS=-DNDEBUG in the configure command environment, rewrite a clean synthetic wrapper successfully, and reject a wrapper with the Worker-local include path reinserted.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           recipe-owned-wrapper-flags
rec_description:        Override CPPFLAGS in the recipe's configure command environment with the minimal target-neutral value required by the package, before configure snapshots WRAPPER_CPPFLAGS. Keep a package-time forbidden-path scan as a fail-closed backstop.
rec_command:            Set CPPFLAGS=-DNDEBUG in the isolated MPICH native environment; run py_compile, the wrapper CPPFLAGS poison fixture, Pre-PR contract, independent W4, current-HEAD Review, and exact-current-HEAD CI.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-autotools-wrapper-relocation

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      structured-wrapper-flag-sanitization
fallback_description:   If target-specific include flags are required, parse the flag vector and retain only paths bound to the package or SDK; do not use substring replacement over the finished script.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       replace\(.*/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local
forbid_1_reason:        Post-generation substring deletion can corrupt unrelated arguments and only handles one Worker layout.
forbid_1_consequence:   A different Worker prefix or quoted flag spelling can leak into the published wrapper.

forbid_2_pattern:       contains non-relocatable paths.*(warn|pass|return)
forbid_2_reason:        Downgrading the relocation guard publishes a wrapper that depends on the build Worker filesystem.
forbid_2_consequence:   Consumers fail after package relocation or resolve unintended user-local headers.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E236]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E328.md
last_updated:           2026-08-17
source_event:           MPICH 5.0.1.2 Buildbot 26312 failed after upstream tests because the OHOS profile CPPFLAGS was persisted in mpicc

